{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Limb (a) of the baseline no-show test is satisfied: the trip record for TRP-09101 carries a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-09-01T08:10:20+08:00, and the driver is the party who terminated the trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (b) is satisfied on the arrival geofence test. All 33 driver fixes sit 24.01 m from the pickup pin - min, mean and max are the same 24.01 m figure - well inside the 50 m arrival radius for a STANDARD zone class. The trace opens at 08:10:00, twenty seconds BEFORE the 08:10:20 'arrived' event, so the driver was inside the geofence at or before that event as the clause requires. Qualifying driver fixes number 33 of 33, so there are far more than the three consecutive in-radius readings POL-NS-02 demands.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (c) is satisfied. The driver's longest qualifying in-geofence run is 320 continuous seconds, from the first qualifying fix at 08:10:00 to the last at 08:15:20, against a STANDARD minimum dwell of 300 seconds. The derived shortfall is MINUS 20 seconds - that is, a 20 second surplus, not a shortfall. The point is robust even on the driver's own less favourable reading: measured from the 'arrived' marker at 08:10:20 to cancellation at 08:15:20 is exactly 300 seconds, still at the minimum. The dwell is measured from the first qualifying GPS fix, per the clause, and not from the arrival tap.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (d) is satisfied. The trip record shows the trip terminated by the driver at 08:15:20 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW - one of the three codes limb (d) expressly recognises - at the very moment the 320 second dwell elapsed, and it records no boarding event anywhere.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09101", "EV-GPS-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival marker is TRUE, so POL-NS-05 does not displace the fee. At the arrived timestamp the trace reports a single distinct speed of 0.0 kph - the driver was stationary, not travelling - and his position was 24 m from the pin, roughly one twelfth of the 300 m distance threshold and nowhere near the 15 kph motion threshold. This is not a driver tapping 'arrived' while rolling down an expressway; it is a driver parked at the pickup point.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-03 is not engaged. The driver was inside the arrival radius, not at a wrong face of the venue 400 m away, so the wrong-entrance route does not arise. Independently, the driver's in-app message at 08:10:35 states he is 'at the sheltered pickup point beside Block 310', and the trip record's registered pickup bears venue_id VEN-CLEMENTI-310 with the label 'Blk 310 Clementi Ave 4, sheltered pickup point'. That is a party statement in the chat log matching the registered venue, not an inference from geography.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09101", "EV-GPS-09101", "EV-CHAT-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider, because limb (a) fails outright. The chat log for the waiting window contains no rider message at all: three messages only - the system notice 'Your driver has arrived' at 08:10:21, and two driver messages at 08:10:35 and 08:14:10. Limb (a) requires at least one locating or coordinating message FROM THE RIDER, and there is none. The message_count of 3 in the chat log also matches trip_record.chat_message_count of 3, so the log is not truncated.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own track does not place them at the pickup point, and cannot support limb (c) of POL-NS-04 either. The rider track carries 15 fixes and rider_qualifying_fix_count is 0 of 15; every fix sits 519.37 m from the pin, far outside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius. I put it precisely: whether those fixes are excluded because they fall outside the radius or are filtered for accuracy, limb (c) is at best undecidable and neutral and at worst affirmatively failed on admissible fixes - on no reading does it place the rider within 100 m of the pin. The rider's assertion that they were 'downstairs' is not borne out by their own device.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no waiting-period shortfall, so POL-NS-06 is not engaged and the fee is not refundable on that route. I disclose that the traffic advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-09101-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT - no advisory matched this pickup road and waiting window. The driver does not rely on limb (i) accumulation and does not need to: the dwell was one single continuous in-geofence run of 320 seconds, so no advisory is required to join intervals together, and I assert nothing against the missing artifact.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09101-01", "EV-GPS-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The money reconciles. The SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is the GREATER of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) under fee_schedule.resolution_rule; the two dimensions agree, the fare breakdown's difference field reads 0.00, and no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect arises. The fee therefore stands as itemised.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.schedule_fee",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No artifact that carries a deciding fact is impaired, so POL-NS-09(a) and (e) are not engaged. The trace is COMPLETE at weight 1.0: 100 per cent coverage, 33 fixes at a 10 second cadence equal to the expected interval, zero gaps and a maximum gap of 0 seconds. The 08:10:20 'arrived' event coincides exactly with a fix, so there is no clock skew under POL-NS-08(a); the log's 3 messages match the trip record, so there is no POL-NS-08(c) chat defect; and the fee reconciles under POL-NS-08(d). Deciding facts rest on clean, weight-1.0 artifacts.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09101", "EV-CHAT-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101", "EV-FARE-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-NS-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No abuse or repeat-dispute trigger is present. rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0, so POL-NS-09(c) is not met; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, so POL-NS-09(d) is not met. I cite only the fields the clause names.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09101", "EV-DPROF-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver is entitled to compensation. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, so POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80 per cent of the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee - SGD 3.20 - with SGD 0.80 retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4, so the second limb is never reached and compensation is not withheld. I rely only on the two fields POL-NS-07 names, no_show_terminations_30d and completed_trips_30d; prior_no_show_flags is a lifetime counter and I do not use it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09101", "EV-DPROF-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the charge itself the disposition is that the present state stands: fare_breakdown shows payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and the evidence does not support the rider's claim to have the charge reversed. Under POL-GEN-03 that is NO_ACTION on the fee, while the case as a whole produces DRIVER_COMPENSATION of SGD 3.20 in the driver's favour.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.2,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.2,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation charge stands, and the driver is paid SGD 3.20 of it.\n\nChargeability turns on POL-NS-01, and all four limbs hold on the same record. (a) EV-TRIP-09101 carries a driver 'arrived' event at 08:10:20. (b) EV-GPS-09101 places the driver 24.01 m from the pickup pin on every one of its 33 fixes - inside the 50 m arrival radius for the STANDARD zone class - and its first fix at 08:10:00 is 20 seconds before the 'arrived' event, satisfying POL-NS-02. (c) The single continuous in-geofence run lasts 320 seconds from the first qualifying fix to the 08:15:20 cancellation, against the 300-second STANDARD minimum; the derived shortfall is minus 20 seconds, i.e. a 20-second surplus, and the dwell is measured from the GPS fix as the clause requires, not from the arrival tap. (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 08:15:20 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes limb (d) recognises, at or after the moment the dwell elapsed, and no boarding event is recorded.\n\nNo clause displaces the fee. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) cannot fire: the driver was inside the arrival radius, not outside it. POL-NS-04 cannot fire: the three messages in EV-CHAT-09101 are the system arrival notice and two driver messages, so limb (a)'s rider locating or coordinating message is absent, and the driver replied 14 seconds after the arrival notice, defeating limb (b) independently. POL-NS-05 cannot fire: at the arrival timestamp the driver was 24 m from the pin at 0.0 km/h, neither beyond the 300 m mark nor moving at 15 km/h. POL-NS-06 cannot fire for the same 320-second reason, and the driver expressly did not assert POL-NS-06(i) against the MISSING advisory EV-ADVIS-09101-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so that clause's escalation trigger is not engaged.\n\nThe SGD 4.00 is the GREATER of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) under fee_schedule.resolution_rule, and fare breakdown's difference field reads 0.00, so no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect arises. POL-NS-07 therefore pays the driver 80 percent of SGD 4.00, which is SGD 3.20, with SGD 0.80 retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4, so the second limb is never reached. Per POL-GEN-03, on this ruling amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.20 figure as driver_compensation_sgd: it is the amount the ruling moves, and the rider's SGD 4.00 charge stands.\n\nThe rider's account that he was 'downstairs' but could not see the car is not borne out by his own device: the 15 rider fixes in EV-GPS-09101 all sit about 519 m from the pin, outside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius, and the chat log contains no rider message in the waiting window. The rider's point that the bundle omits per-fix accuracy readings would at most make POL-NS-04 limb (c) undecidable rather than failed; it cannot rescue the clause, because limbs (a) and (b) fail independently.\n\nNo escalation trigger is met under POL-NS-09: confidence is above the 0.70 floor; no admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles; no_show_disputes_30d is 0; and no deciding fact rests on an impaired artifact - the trace is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 with 100 percent coverage, 33 fixes at the expected 10-second cadence and no gaps, the chat log carries the 3 messages the trip record counts, and the fee reconciles. The referee's flag that the driver's claim mentions the context-only field prior_no_show_flags does not require a discard: the claim cites it only to say it is not relied on, and it reasons instead from no_show_terminations_30d and completed_trips_30d, the two fields POL-NS-07 names. No clause in this category produces a referral on these facts, so there is none."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.20,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.20,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation charge stands, it is not refunded, and SGD 3.20 of it is paid to the driver. To the driver: your fee is upheld and you are compensated.\n\nWhy the charge stands. The POL-NS-01 baseline test is met on all four limbs. (a) The trip record for TRP-09101 carries a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-09-01T08:10:20+08:00. (b) The GPS trace EV-GPS-09101 places the driver 24.0 m from the pickup pin — well inside the 50 m arrival radius for a STANDARD zone — on all 33 fixes, the first at 08:10:00, twenty seconds BEFORE the arrival event, so the driver was in the geofence at or before it. (c) The driver held position for one continuous 320-second run, from the first qualifying fix at 08:10:00 to the 08:15:20 cancellation, against the 300-second STANDARD minimum (POL-NS-06 fixes the minimum); the derived shortfall is MINUS 20 seconds, a surplus. Measured from the arrival tap it is still exactly 300 seconds. (d) The trip record shows no boarding and termination by the driver with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes limb (d) recognises, at 08:15:20 — after the required dwell elapsed at 08:15:00.\n\nWhy no rider-side clause displaces the fee. POL-NS-03 does not fire: the driver was inside the arrival radius, not at a wrong face of the venue within the 400 m ceiling. POL-NS-05 does not fire: at the arrival marker the driver was stationary at 0 km/h and 24 m from the pin — neither more than 300 m away nor travelling at 15 km/h or above — so the marker is TRUE and the waiting clock is not recomputed. POL-NS-06 does not fire: there is no shortfall to refund, and the only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-09101-01, is MISSING at weight 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT; the driver disclosed that impairment and asserts nothing against it, and no advisory is needed because the dwell was a single continuous interval, not summed intervals. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: the chat log holds three messages and none is from the rider, so limb (a) fails; the driver replied 14 seconds after the arrival notice and again at 08:14:10, so limb (b) fails; and the rider's own device sits about 519 m from the pin on all 15 fixes, outside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius, so limb (c) fails on any reading. Your account that you were 'downstairs' is not borne out by your own device, and you sent no locating or coordinating message during the waiting window; rider presence is not a condition of the no-show fee, so this does not change the outcome.\n\nOn the money. The SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is the GREATER of the SGD 4.00 STANDARD zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee, so the fare line reconciles and no POL-NS-08(d) defect arises. Because POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80 percent of SGD 4.00 = SGD 3.20, with SGD 0.80 retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4, so compensation is paid and not withheld. No POL-NS-09 trigger applies: no admissible artifacts contradict one another on arrival, dwell or rider presence; disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles; no_show_disputes_30d is 0; and no artifact carrying a deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d). The driver's claim cited prior_no_show_flags only to state he was not relying on it, consistent with POL-GEN-01. No clause produces a referral, so none is recorded.\n\nConfidence. The deciding facts (arrival, dwell, termination, fee amount) are carried by weight-1.0 artifacts — the trip record, the GPS trace and the fare breakdown — so the cap is 1.0; confidence is stated at 0.95."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
